Readme

InviteOnWhisper lets you automate invites from custom keywords in whispers or chat channels. Players must set the keywords themselves before it will do anything.
Setup

    Type /iow info to see the current configuration.

    Set one or more keywords with the /iow commands.

    When another player uses a matching keyword, the addon will invite them.

Commands

    /iow info shows the current settings and help text.

    /iow whisperguild <text> sets the whisper keyword for guild invite requests.

    /iow whisperparty <text> sets the whisper keyword for party invite requests.

    /iow guildkeyword <text> sets the channel keyword for guild invite requests.

    /iow partykeyword <text> sets the channel keyword for party invite requests.

    /iow blacklist <name> blocks a player from using the addon.

    /iow unblacklist <name> removes a player from the blacklist.

    /iow bl lists blacklisted names.

Example

If you set:

    /iow whisperparty partyme

    /iow whisperguild guildme

then a whisper of partyme will invite the player to your party, and a whisper of guildme will trigger a guild invite request.
